## §3 — Skills (G3)

### 3.1 — Design

Skills follow pi's `SKILL.md` convention: markdown files with YAML frontmatter,
discovered at session init, injected into the system prompt.

**No core changes**. `SystemPromptFn` closure already supports this — G3 decision
(see `01-core-design.md` §7).

### 3.2 — SKILL.md Format

```markdown
---
name: "rust-refactor"
description: "Rust code refactoring: extract function, simplify match, use combinators"
disable-model-invocation: false
---

## Guidelines
- Prefer `match` over `if let` chains
- Extract closures ≥5 lines into named functions
...
```

### 3.3 — Loading Mechanism

```go
// pkg/coding/skills/loader.go
type SkillLoader struct {
    dirs []string // ~/.tau/skills/, .tau/skills/, project .tau/skills/
}

type Skill struct {
    Name        string
    Description string
    Content     string   // full markdown body
    SourcePath  string
    DisableInvocation bool
}

func (l *SkillLoader) Load() ([]Skill, error)
```

### 3.4 — Injection into System Prompt

The `SystemPromptFn` closure:

```go
loader := skills.NewLoader(dirs)
systemPrompt := func(sess *core.Session) (string, error) {
    skills, _ := loader.Load()
    return prompts.BuildSystemPrompt(prompts.BuildInput{
        Skills:       skills,
        WorkspaceRoot: workspaceRoot,
        ToolSchemas:   sess.Tools.Active(),
    }), nil
}
```

Skills appear in system prompt as:

```
## Available Skills

You may invoke skills by name. When you invoke a skill, its full content will be loaded.

- rust-refactor: Rust code refactoring (extract function, simplify match, use combinators)
- python-testing: Python test patterns with pytest
```

When an LLM response invokes a skill (e.g., "I'll use the rust-refactor skill"), the
product layer appends the skill's full body to the next turn's context.

### 3.5 — Discovery Order

1. Built-in skills: embedded via `embed.FS`, always available
2. User skills: `~/.tau/skills/`
3. Project skills: `<workspace>/.tau/skills/`

Later directories override earlier (same `name` → last wins).

