## §5 — CLI Design

### 5.1 — Entry Point

```
cmd/tau/main.go
```

Single binary: `tau`. Subcommands planned (v1: implicit coding-agent mode).

### 5.2 — Arguments (v1)

```
tau [flags] [prompt...]

Flags:
  --provider <name>        Provider name (default: "openai" from TAU_PROVIDER)
  --model <model>          Model name (default: from provider)
  --api-key <key>          API key (env: TAU_API_KEY)
  --workspace <dir>        Workspace root (default: .)
  --system-prompt <file>   Override system prompt template
  --skills-dir <dir>       Additional skills directory (repeatable)
  --no-skills              Disable skill loading
  --continue, -c           Continue last session
  --resume <id>            Resume specific session
  --no-tools               Disable all tools
  --verbose, -v            Verbose output
```

### 5.3 — Flow

```
1. Parse args
2. Resolve workspace root (--workspace flag → TAU_WORKSPACE env → cwd)
3. Load skills (unless --no-skills)
4. Build SessionOptions{SystemPrompt: closure, Provider: ..., DefaultModel: ...}
5. sess := core.NewSession(ctx, opts)
6. sess.Providers.RegisterVendor(providerName, cfg)
7. Register 7 tools → sess.Tools
8. Register hooks (TransformContext, BeforeToolCall for permission gate)
9. loop := core.NewLoop()
10. run, _ := loop.Prompt(ctx, sess, core.UserInput{Text: prompt})
11. Stream run.Events to TUI (Phase 5+)
12. block on run.Done()
```

