## §6 — Core Access Point Mapping

All 11 access points (from `05-access-points.md`), mapped to coding-agent usage:

| # | AP | Coding-Agent Usage |
|---|----|--------------------|
| 1 | `sess.Tools.Register` | Register 7 tools at session init |
| 2 | `sess.Tools.SetActive` | Dynamic enable/disable (--no-tools flag) |
| 3 | `sess.Hooks.BeforeToolCall` | Permission gate: confirm destructive ops |
| 4 | `sess.Hooks.AfterToolCall` | File-op extraction for compaction context |
| 5 | `SystemPromptFn` | Skills injection + base prompt template |
| 6 | `run.Events` | TUI streaming: MessageDelta → render, ToolCallEnd → show result |
| 7 | `sess.Transcript.Subscribe` | Multi-client webui watching same session |
| 8 | `run.Done()` | Batch mode: block on final result |
| 9 | `core.NewSession` | One session per CLI invocation |
| 10 | `sess.Providers.RegisterVendor` | Register OpenAI/Anthropic/OpenRouter at startup |
| 11 | `Provider.Complete` | Compaction summarization, skill content generation |

All 11 consumed. Zero new core access points needed.

